Interface            How you use it                 Advantages                        Disadvantages
-------------------  -----------------------------  --------------------------------  ---------------------------------
GUI (graphical)      Windows, icons, menus, pointer  Easy to learn; no commands to      Needs more RAM/processing power;
                     (WIMP), touch                   memorise; visual feedback          slower for expert repetitive jobs
Command line (CLI)   Type text commands             Fast for experts; low power needs; Must memorise exact commands;
                                                    can be scripted/automated          hard for beginners; typos fail
Menu-driven          Pick from a list of options    Very simple; no training needed    Slow to reach deep options; limited
                     (cash machine, old TV menus)                                      to what the menus offer
Voice                Speak commands (smart speaker)  Hands-free; accessible for some    Misunderstands accents/noise;
                                                    disabilities; natural              privacy concerns; limited commands
